.TH DMN-BLUETOOTH-CLI 1 "2026" "Dmn" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
dmn-bluetooth-cli \- monitor notifications from a selected iPhone using ANCS
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B dmn-bluetooth-cli monitor
.I DEVICE
[
.B --adapter
.I ADAPTER
]
[
.B --discovery-timeout
.I SECONDS
]
[
.B --pair-timeout
.I SECONDS
]
[
.B --connect-timeout
.I SECONDS
]
[
.B --services-timeout
.I SECONDS
]
[
.B --unlimited
]
[
.B --ignore-existing
]
.br
.B dmn-bluetooth-cli --help
.br
.B dmn-bluetooth-cli monitor --help
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B dmn-bluetooth-cli
connects to one selected Bluetooth device, establishes an Apple Notification
Center Service (ANCS) session, and prints notification events and available
attributes to standard output. Progress and diagnostics are written to
standard error.
.PP
.I DEVICE
is a Bluetooth address or exact BlueZ display name. A name must resolve to
exactly one known device; ambiguous names are rejected. If the device is not
known to BlueZ, the application performs bounded discovery to find it.
.PP
The command explicitly pairs the selected device if necessary and then
connects it. It does not pair or connect to other discovery results. Normal
exit and failure leave the pairing and connection in place.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI "--adapter " ADAPTER
Select a local adapter by its Bluetooth address or current BlueZ object path.
If omitted, the application selects an adapter when the selection is
unambiguous.
.TP
.BI "--discovery-timeout " SECONDS
Maximum time to discover a device that is not already known to BlueZ.
Default: 30 seconds.
.TP
.BI "--pair-timeout " SECONDS
Maximum time allowed for pairing through BlueZ's configured default agent.
Default: 120 seconds.
.TP
.BI "--connect-timeout " SECONDS
Maximum time allowed for the selected device to connect. Default: 30 seconds.
.TP
.BI "--services-timeout " SECONDS
Maximum time to wait for BlueZ to resolve services. Default: 30 seconds.
.TP
.B --unlimited
Disable the cap on queued notification attribute requests. Without this
option, the oldest pending notifications are discarded when the bounded queue
is full.
.TP
.B --ignore-existing
Suppress completed notification details whose ANCS date is older than the
application process start time. Notifications with missing or unrecognized
dates are also suppressed. The ANCS date has no timezone, so the phone and
host clocks should be aligned.
.TP
.B --help
Print usage and exit without contacting D-Bus.
.PP
Timeout values must be positive whole seconds no greater than 600.
.SH OUTPUT
Notification events are printed as they arrive during the current monitoring
session; the application is not a notification-history store. Available
attributes include app identifier, title, subtitle, message, and date. Missing
attributes are omitted. Notification content is written to standard output;
diagnostics are written to standard error and do not include notification
bodies.
.PP
The application becomes ready only after it finds the ANCS service and its
required characteristics and confirms that notifications are active on both
ANCS characteristics. BlueZ reporting a connected device or resolved
services alone does not establish ANCS readiness.
.SH RECOVERY
If ANCS is missing after a previous pairing, disconnecting and reconnecting
from Linux may not clear stale GATT state. An observed recovery was to remove
the Pop!_OS pairing from the iPhone, then pair again and retry monitoring.
This removes the existing bond and requires pairing again; the command never
does this automatically.
.PP
If BlueZ accepts a notification subscription but reports notifications
inactive, or the session fails with a D-Bus timeout, the command reports the
failure and exits rather than claiming that monitoring is active. Retry only
after checking the BlueZ connection and pairing state.
.SH EXAMPLES
Monitor a device by exact display name:
.PP
.nf
dmn-bluetooth-cli monitor "iPhone Genghis"
.fi
.PP
Monitor a device by Bluetooth address and select an adapter:
.PP
.nf
dmn-bluetooth-cli monitor 84:D3:28:96:72:9A --adapter /org/bluez/hci0
.fi
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Monitoring stopped successfully or help was printed.
.TP
.B 2
Invalid, unknown, duplicate, or incomplete command-line option.
.TP
.B 3
BlueZ is unavailable or its service owner disappeared.
.TP
.B 4
The selected device could not be resolved uniquely.
.TP
.B 5
Pairing or connection failed.
.TP
.B 6
ANCS service or required characteristics are unavailable.
.TP
.B 7
ANCS session startup failed.
.TP
.B 8
Runtime, protocol, or cleanup failure.
